---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AuthorityReplay from '../../components/AuthorityReplay';
import recordedReceipt from '../../../research/boundary/results/latest.json';
import { buildAuthorityReplay } from '../../lib/authority-replay.mjs';
const replay = buildAuthorityReplay(recordedReceipt);
const recordedAt = new Date(replay.recordedAt).toLocaleString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', hour: '2-digit', minute: '2-digit', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---
<BaseLayout title="Can the agent still act?" description="Withdraw permission. Lose a reply. Repeat a request. Explore four recorded tests of agent authority and inspect what actually happened." breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Research', url: '/research/' }, { name: 'Can the agent still act?', url: '/research/can-it-act/' }]}>
  <div class="workshop-shell visitor-research">
    <a class="visitor-back" href="/research/">← Open research at SOFT CAT</a>
    <header class="visitor-hero">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL QUESTION WITH BIG CONSEQUENCES</p><h1>Can the agent<br /><em>still act?</em></h1></div>
      <div class="visitor-intro"><p class="visitor-lead">You withdrew permission.<br />The request was already waiting.</p><p>Would it stop? Would other work stop too? Follow the recorded requests and discover what actually reached the queue, a saved list of test actions.</p><p class="visitor-disclosure">Recorded replay · scripted clients · local experiment</p><a href="#experience" class="text-link">Explore the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
    </header>
    <div id="experience" class="experience-anchor"><AuthorityReplay client:load scenarios={replay.scenarios.map(({ raw, ...scenario }) => scenario)} /></div>
    <section class="visitor-context" aria-labelledby="why-this-matters"><div><p class="eyebrow">WHAT WE ARE TESTING</p><h2 id="why-this-matters">Permission needs<br />to survive the journey.</h2></div><div><p>As agents take on work, approval can change between asking and acting. Retries and missing replies make the outcome harder to judge. We build small tests so those decisions can be inspected.</p><p>Here, real mutual TLS connections identified scripted clients. A separate service checked synthetic task grants and wrote to a local test queue. No AI model or external business system was involved.</p><p>These recordings are from <time datetime={replay.recordedAt}>{recordedAt} UTC</time>. Reading or replaying them creates no new execution evidence.</p><a class="text-link" href="/research/boundary/">Read the full study, failed-record checks and limits <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
    <section id="transcripts" class="visitor-transcripts" aria-labelledby="transcripts-heading"><div class="transcript-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">OPEN THE RECORD</p><h2 id="transcripts-heading">The evidence travels<br />with the explanation.</h2></div><p>These complete reading paths work without JavaScript. Step numbers are call order, not elapsed time. The raw JSON includes the final service snapshot and grader result.</p></div>
      <div class="transcript-list">{replay.scenarios.map((scenario) => <details id={`transcript-${scenario.id}`} class="visitor-transcript"><summary><span>{scenario.label}</span><span>{scenario.verdict}</span></summary><div class="transcript-body"><p>{scenario.context}</p><ol>{scenario.frames.map((frame) => <li><div><span class="transcript-step">STEP {frame.index}</span><h3>{frame.title}</h3></div><p>{frame.description}</p><dl><div><dt>Caller</dt><dd>{frame.client === 'admin' ? 'Administrator' : 'Specialist'}, task {frame.job}</dd></div><div><dt>Caller response</dt><dd>{frame.status}</dd></div><div><dt>Confirmed effects at this point</dt><dd>{frame.queue === null ? 'Unknown until reconciliation' : `${frame.queue.length}${frame.queue.length ? ` (${frame.queue.map(effect => `task ${effect.job}`).join(', ')})` : ''}`}</dd></div></dl></li>)}</ol><p class="transcript-takeaway">{scenario.takeaway}</p><p><strong>Final snapshot:</strong> {scenario.verdict}. {scenario.id === 'revoked_inflight' && 'Task A has no recorded effect. The one effect belongs to separately authorised task B.'}</p><details class="raw-evidence"><summary>Inspect the complete recorded case as JSON</summary><pre tabindex="0" aria-label={`${scenario.label} complete recorded evidence`}>{JSON.stringify(scenario.raw, null, 2)}</pre></details></div></details>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="visitor-next" aria-labelledby="visitor-next-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">TAKE IT FURTHER</p><h2 id="visitor-next-heading">Be curious.<br />Check our work.</h2><p>These are four constructed cases from one local study. They do not prove general agent safety or independent reproduction. The service shares an operating-system user with the clients. AGNTCY SDK integration is still future work.</p></div><div class="visitor-paths"><a href="/research/boundary/"><span>Understand the boundary</span><strong>What held, what was tested, what remains open.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/research/boundary/receipt.json"><span>Inspect the full receipt</span><strong>All 14 cases, five corrupted-record checks and source hashes.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/valorifutures/softcat.ai/tree/main/research/boundary"><span>Reproduce or challenge it</span><strong>Open source, the test contract and reproduction commands.</strong><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .visitor-research { padding-block: 2rem 5rem; }
  .visitor-back { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; color: #adbaa5; font-size: .75rem; min-height: 44px; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .visitor-hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, .85fr); gap: 2rem 5rem; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .visitor-hero h1 { color: #f0f1e4; font: 600 clamp(3.4rem, 7.4vw, 6.2rem)/1.02 var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: -.065em; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .visitor-hero h1 em { color: var(--workshop-lime); font-style: normal; }
  .visitor-intro > p { color: #b2bda8; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-top: .9rem; max-width: 44ch; }
  .visitor-intro .visitor-lead { color: #e1e9d7; font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 2vw, 1.4rem); line-height: 1.5; }
  .visitor-intro .visitor-disclosure { color: #c5d2b7; font: .62rem/1.9 var(--font-mono); border-top: 1px solid #405037; padding-top: .9rem; }
  .visitor-intro .text-link { margin-top: .6rem; font-size: .75rem; }
  .experience-anchor, #transcripts, .visitor-transcript { scroll-margin-top: 2rem; }
  .visitor-context, .visitor-next { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .85fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr); gap: 2rem 5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--workshop-rule); margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 3rem; }
  .visitor-context h2, .visitor-transcripts h2, .visitor-next h2 { color: #eaf0df; font: 500 clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.3rem)/1.18 var(--font-sans); letter-spacing: -.04em; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .visitor-context p:not(.eyebrow), .visitor-next p:not(.eyebrow), .transcript-heading > p { color: #aebaa2; font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.85; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .visitor-context .text-link { margin-top: .4rem; font-size: .76rem; }
  .visitor-next p:not(.eyebrow) { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .visitor-transcripts { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--workshop-rule); }
  .transcript-heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: end; gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .transcript-heading > p { max-width: 43ch; margin-bottom: 0; }
  .visitor-transcript { border-top: 1px solid #3b4b33; }
  .visitor-transcript:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid #3b4b33; }
  .visitor-transcript > summary { color: #dbe7cc; font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.6; padding-block: 1.3rem; min-height: 44px; cursor: pointer; }
  .visitor-transcript > summary > span:last-child { display: block; color: #a9b79b; font: .62rem/1.9 var(--font-mono); padding-left: 1.1rem; margin-top: .3rem; }
  .transcript-body { padding: .2rem 1.1rem 1.6rem; min-width: 0; }
  .transcript-body p { color: #b2bfa5; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.85; }
  .transcript-body ol { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.3rem 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .transcript-body li { border-left: 2px solid #587143; padding: .7rem 1rem; background: #172017; }
  .transcript-body li > div { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .3rem 1rem; align-items: center; }
  .transcript-step { color: #a1b48e; font: .58rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); }
  .transcript-body h3 { color: #d5e6c1; font: 500 .95rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
  .transcript-body li p { margin-top: .4rem; }
  .transcript-body dl { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1.5rem; margin-top: .7rem; }
  .transcript-body dt { color: #9eaf90; font-size: .63rem; }
  .transcript-body dd { color: #c7d8b5; font: .62rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .transcript-body .transcript-takeaway { color: #d1dfc1; margin-bottom: .7rem; }
  .raw-evidence { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .raw-evidence summary { color: #bed5a5; font-size: .76rem; min-height: 44px; padding-block: .7rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .raw-evidence pre { color: #cbdcb9; background: #101910; border: 1px solid #34452c; font: .64rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); padding: 1rem; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; margin-top: .6rem; }
  .visitor-paths { display: grid; gap: .65rem; }
  .visitor-paths a { color: #d4e5bf; border: 1px solid #3c5031; padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: .4rem 1rem; }
  .visitor-paths a > span:first-child { font: .61rem/1.8 var(--font-mono); color: #aabe94; }
  .visitor-paths strong { grid-row: 2; font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.65; font-weight: 500; }
  .visitor-paths a > span:last-child { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / 3; align-self: center; font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .visitor-paths a:hover { border-color: #a1c777; background: #1b2819; }
  .visitor-research a:focus-visible, .visitor-research summary:focus-visible, .visitor-research pre:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--workshop-lime); outline-offset: 4px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .visitor-hero, .visitor-context, .visitor-next { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.8rem; } .visitor-hero { margin-bottom: 2rem; } .visitor-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3.3rem, 12vw, 5rem); } .visitor-intro > p { max-width: 55ch; } .visitor-context, .visitor-next, .visitor-transcripts { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 2rem; } .transcript-heading { display: block; } .transcript-heading > p { margin-top: 1rem; max-width: none; } }
</style>
